# Trivy vulnerability exceptions for the Docker image built from api/Dockerfile.
# Add a CVE ID per line with a comment explaining why it's accepted, e.g.:
# CVE-2023-12345  # false positive, not reachable in our usage — see <link>

# brace-expansion DoS (memory exhaustion via crafted pattern), fixed upstream
# in 5.0.8 — but the vulnerable copy here is the one *vendored inside the
# globally-installed npm CLI itself* (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/
# node_modules/brace-expansion), not a dependency of our app. That npm is
# only invoked manually by the site operator for `npm run migration:run`/
# `seed` (see api/Dockerfile) — never fed attacker-controlled input over the
# network, so the DoS path (arbitrary strings into brace-expansion.expand())
# isn't reachable in this deployment. Re-check next time api/Dockerfile's
# base image or `npm install -g npm@latest` step changes, in case npm has
# picked up the fixed brace-expansion by then.
CVE-2026-14257
